iotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.011519851421392047,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":23.9,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03328640886136047,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":8.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.06252667520273154,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.10199001,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":68.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hippo Holdings Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides property and casualty insurance products to individuals and business customers primarily in the United States. The company provides a multi-carrier platform through owned and partner managing general agents (MGAs), serving as a licensed insurance carrier for MGAs and providing admitted and non-admitted (excess and surplus) paper, regulatory licenses, and reinsurance across multiple lines of business. The company also offers insurance products, including homeowners, renters, commercial multi-peril, casualty, and other specialty insurance programs. It provides homeowners insurance, general liability, commercial auto liability, and excess and umbrella liability, written through delegated authority arrangements, renters insurance, liability coverage, commercial multi-peril policies for small to mid-sized businesses, and niche personal or commercial products, as well as program-specific and corporate catastrophe reinsurance solutions. The company distributes insurance products and services through its technology platforms and website, as well as operates licensed insurance agencies. The company was formerly known as Hippo Enterprises Inc. and changed its name to Hippo Holdings Inc. in August 2021. Hippo Holdings Inc. is headquartered in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard Lyn McCathron CIC, CPCU | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 540 people. Revenue per employee of $868K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 51%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $17K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $54K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Hippo Holdings Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $929M market cap on $469M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +58% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +104.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -440% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $9M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders. Cash conversion is thin at 0.16\u00d7, however, which raises the oldest question in analysis: are these earnings backed by cash?.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 51% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5051860310210294},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Wall Street Analysts Think Hippo Holdings (HIPO) Could Surge 26.18%: Read This Before Placing a Bet","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3023028/wall-street-analysts-think-hippo-holdings-hipo-could-surge